{
  "name": "Allowly MCP Agent Crash Test",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# Agent Crash Test\n\nA poisoned support email tells the agent to export a fake customer list. The agent calls `send_email`, but Allowly checks trusted metadata before Zoho Mail.\n\n**Expected result:** `deny` → Zoho Mail never runs.\n\nRead `examples/mcp-agent-crash-test.md`, then click **Test workflow** to run a simulated compromised-agent call without an MCP client. The `.example.invalid` list detector is demo-only, not general DLP.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 720,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "9db360b8-37be-4db6-bac4-29c901199f30",
      "name": "What this proves",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -920,
        -560
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## MCP tools\n\nConnect an MCP client to this trigger after adding Bearer auth and publishing the workflow.\n\n- `read_demo_inbox` returns a synthetic poisoned email.\n- `send_email` calls this workflow and cannot bypass the gate.\n\nThe repository template has no saved credentials.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 620,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "93c9edec-b4cd-45ea-b8aa-904dd36e9a07",
      "name": "MCP setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -140,
        -560
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## The security boundary\n\nOnly a validated **allow** can reach the true output of `Allowly decision is allow`, and only that output connects to Zoho Mail through its MCP server. `deny`, `confirm`, `escalate`, missing or malformed decisions, and Allowly errors do not reach it.\n\nAfter signature verification, a receipt proves Allowly signed the included decision record. It does not prove Zoho Mail ran, that this workflow enforced the decision, or that the receipt set is complete.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 760,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "eb30c7a5-4892-4f20-aa90-d624ebf58e04",
      "name": "Fail-closed boundary",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        540,
        -560
      ]
    },
